This is a midstream draft of the fd-based /boot finalize fix for bootc#2402. The design follows the operator's review on upstream ostree PR 3689.

- **Finalize** reads and writes the boot filesystem through `/sysroot/boot` when `/boot` is on the physical root. Writes go through a private writable `open_tree(OPEN_TREE_CLONE)` mount. Kernels without the new mount API fall back to the old remount.
- **`finalize-staged --hold`** now holds `/boot` open itself.

